# The browser harness lives in test/browser beside the unit tests. Its inputs — the probes and the seed
# fixtures that carry a frozen clock — are tracked, because a failing probe with no baseline to diff against
# is the problem moving the unit tests was meant to solve. Everything it generates is not.
# dbg-<page>.html is built from test/browser/seed/ on every probe run; the seed is the input that is kept.
test/browser/dbg-*.html
test/browser/al-*.html
test/browser/fl-*.html
test/browser/fl2-*.html
test/browser/dbg2-*.html
test/browser/host-*.html
test/browser/ph-*.html
test/browser/*.png

# Lavish review artifacts: generated for a conversation, not part of the app.
.lavish/

# Agent skills, not app. These are generic tooling — Lavish, gh, a task backlog, a quota reporter — that
# happen to be checked out here because .claude/skills is the only place a project-local skill can live.
# None of them is about HQ, and a tracked dot-directory is served: .impeccable/brief-body.md answers 200 on
# the live site. They keep working untracked.
.claude/
